  <Placemark>
    <description><![CDATA[<a href="http://www.nv.doe.gov/nts/tours.htm">Sedan Crater</a> is the site of the largest cratering shot in the Plowshare Program. It was as created at the Nevada Test Site on July 6, 1962. A simple 104 kiloton explosive, buried under 635 feet of desert alluvium, displaced 12 million tons of earth and formed a crater 320 feet deep and 1,280 feet in diameter. Follow the link above for information about tours of the area.]]></description>
    <name>Sedan Crater, Nevada</name>
